<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Neutral Confederacy</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1651 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A populous Iroquoian confederacy north of Lake Erie, named Neutral by the French for staying out of the Huron-Iroquois wars until its own destruction in 1651.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Neutral, called Attawandaron by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/huron-confederacy">Huron</a>, developed from Iroquoian farming communities in what is now south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-river-ontario">Grand River</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niagara-river">Niagara River</a>. By the early 17th century they numbered perhaps 30,000 to 40,000 people in around 40 villages, organised as a confederacy of several tribes.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>French observers named them the Neutral Nation because they let both the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/huron-confederacy">Huron Confederacy</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Iroquois Confederacy</a> pass through their lands in peace. They grew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and tobacco, quarried chert on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niagara-escarpment">Niagara Escarpment</a>, and traded with both sides. Under the war chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsouharissen">Tsouharissen</a> in the 1640s they waged campaigns against Algonquian peoples to the west, notably the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mascouten">Mascouten</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/recollects">Recollet</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> missionaries, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-de-brebeuf">Jean de Brébeuf</a> in 1640 to 1641, made few converts.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/huron-confederacy">Huron</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Iroquois Confederacy</a> attacked the Neutral in 1650 and 1651, burning their towns. Thousands were killed or taken captive, and most survivors were absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/seneca-nation">Seneca</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/neutral-confederacy.jpg" alt="Neutral Confederacy" width="320" height="189"><figcaption>Image: The Hsinging Tree · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Neutral_Confederacy_in_1600.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1651 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tsouharissen</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iroquoian traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Neutral</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a>, <a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Attawandaron, Neutral Nation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1576&amp;focus=neutral-confederacy" aria-label="Neutral Confederacy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2560 167 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Neutral Confederacy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3160 908h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2880 423h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2880 423h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Canada. <a href="/atlas?year=1576&amp;focus=neutral-confederacy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

